\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$; the standard number fields have their usual meanings. All additional conventions are stated locally.


\paragraph{Definitions and notation.}In the standard bosonic Fock representation, $a|n\rangle=\sqrt n\,|n-1\rangle$, $a^\dagger|n\rangle=\sqrt{n+1}\,|n+1\rangle$, $[a,a^\dagger]=I$ and the number operator is $N=a^\dagger a$. Thus $aa^\dagger=N+I$. The displayed Hamiltonian is generally unbounded on its natural operator domain. Its spectral behavior depends on the real parameters, including zero-parameter cases.

